<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Banerj court order lifted.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Banerj court order lifted.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rio de Janeiro state government has succeeded in lifting a court injunction that blocked the privatization auction of its state bank Banerj, the Rio Planning Office said.</p>
<p>Planning Secretary Marco Aurelio Alencar is holding a news conference to explain details on the court decision. He may also announce when a new date for the selloff will be set.</p>
<p>Banerj was due to be auctioned off Tuesday but the sale was postponed after a judge granted an injunction to the Association of Banerj's employees, an opponent of the selloff.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina Sao Paulo Newsroom, 55-11-2485412))</p>
